STRING CreditStr "Larn was written by Noah Morgan in 1986.  "\
		"Ularn, \"Ultra-Larn\", by Phil Cordier, is based on "\
		"Larn and was created in 1989 or so.  "\
		"(iLarn is a port of Ularn, so, you have these folks "\
		"to thank or blame for its existence.)\n"\
		"Ularn was later maintained by Josh Brandt.\n"\
		"Thanks also to "\
		"intrepid testers and reporters of bugs.\n"\
		"- Bridget Spitznagel\n\n"\
		"Later:\n"\
		"iLarn 0.30 came out in August 2001, with colour, "\
		"beaming, clones and the message log.  It was the "\
		"last release.\n\n"\
		"In 2026 iLarn was revived as version 0.40 for current "\
		"Palm OS devices and build tools: a built-in neon colour "\
		"scheme, the 5-way navigator of the Tungsten C and other "\
		"Palm OS 5 devices, bug fixes and a manual e-book.  "\
		"Source and bug reports: "\
		"github.com/z88kat/palm-roguelike"
